# Repository boundaries

## Observed systems

### Entity: Contracts

Solidity contracts, ENS adapters/interfaces, tests, and deployment records. Records are not live-health evidence.

```yaml
entity: Contracts
type: component
properties:
  adr:
    default: docs/adrs/0005-trigger-and-settlement.md
  paths:
    default: contracts/
states: [observed]
```

### Entity: Shared

Shared feed and Trigger contracts, computation, exported ABIs, deployment addresses, and the marketplace catalogue/quote builder. Catalogue extraction preserves the existing listing IDs, prices and SaleRouter split. Review together with Solidity when their interface changes.

```yaml
entity: Shared
type: component
properties:
  adr:
    default: docs/adrs/0005-trigger-and-settlement.md
  paths:
    default: packages/shared/
states: [observed]
```

### Entity: Pipeline

Python (uv) FastAPI risk API, Docker/Caddy deployment files, pytest suite and pinned buoy/toxin/geographic inputs. Merged #112 adds pinned JAXA ingestion, heat indices, heat/HAB layers, CLI builds and synthetic demo plot geometry. Q10 defines daily SST fallback with product/pixel provenance. Restriction indices, storm and advisory routes remain incomplete (501); /health reports partial implementation. The TypeScript feed server and signer were removed; signing moves to the keeper (#64).

```yaml
entity: Pipeline
type: component
properties:
  adr:
    default: docs/adrs/0003-risk-api-and-keeper.md
  paths:
    default: pipeline/
states: [observed]
```

### Entity: Application

Current Next.js UI/routes, keeper, wallet/identity flows, event handling, and LINE integration, plus the frontend/ Astro HMI and relief views. The HMI has species-coloured plots, compact layer controls, observed relief thresholds, and hourly forecast playback with a plot-anchored readout. Forecasts remain advisory; recorded temperature is independent of payout rules. The Astro storefront uses the shared catalogue and existing quote-signing service, verifies purchase and relief receipts, and retains pending transactions for recovery. Relief and market views show verified seller/fund splits. Storybook covers panel focus, responsive layouts, filters and language switching. Remaining route and service migration stays under #54.

```yaml
entity: Application
type: component
properties:
  adr:
    default: docs/adrs/0002-astro-and-app-core.md
  paths:
    default: web/ frontend/
states: [observed]
```

